Agent_1 (Trustee):
Myth: After Fallow's return, the three siblings worked in harmony again. The fields flourished under their careful rhythm. But one season, Bloom noticed Fallow's bare fields and felt troubled.

"Sister, you work so hard clearing and resting the earth," Bloom said kindly. "Let me help you. I'll plant flowers to make your season beautiful too."

Before Fallow could respond, Bloom covered the resting fields with winter blossoms. They looked lovely, but their roots drank the nutrients the soil needed to restore. Their leaves blocked the cleansing snows.

When spring arrived, Bloom tried to work—but the exhausted soil yielded only weak shoots. Harvest came to gather, but found little worth taking. The cycle broke again, not from malice but from misplaced kindness.

Quietus came to the confused siblings. "Bloom, your generosity moved your heart. But helping means understanding what another truly needs, not giving what you think they should want."

"Fallow doesn't need your flowers," Verdana added. "She needs the space to do her essential work unseen."

Bloom learned a harder lesson than before: love means respecting another's purpose, even when it looks like absence. True cooperation requires not just working together, but allowing each their necessary season—including the season of rest.
